    "created_at": "2025-03-31T17:42:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-31T17:43:39Z",
    "body": "It looks like the blocking of fish style truncation is happening [here](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/directory.rs#L89-L101) and it is explicitly *not* allowing it when substitutions exist. That said, it claims there are potential issues with a potentially changed prefix.\n\nIn the [function that does the fish-style shortening](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/directory.rs#L318), it is going through the path prefix generated from the raw path [here](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/directory.rs#L93). It seems to me like just removing the substitutions check would allow the fish style shortening to happen while ignoring the substitutions.\n\nI can see a few difference solutions:\n\n1. Add a settings that users can opt into for allowing fish style shortening when substitutions are enabled\n    * not ideal, but I would appreciate that over the current behaviour when I have the same repo cloned in multiple places but still want to use `truncate_to_repo = true` most of the time\n2. Perform the substitutions on each [component](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/directory.rs#L320) of the path\n    * this removes the ability to do big substitutions that include path separator characters, so maybe this should be opt-in too?\n    * useful for substitutions like `\"Documents\" = \"📄\"` which help with shortening the path into something more digestable\n3. Perform the substitutions that include path separators prior to [breaking the path to components](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/directory.rs#L320) and then apply the ones without path separators to each component?\n4. Something else I haven't considered",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
